        "crossComponentResources": [
          "{AppInsights}"
        ],
        "visualization": "table"
      },
      "customWidth": "50",
      "name": "tool-error-rate"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": { "json": "## Provisioned Throughput (PTU) break-even\n**PTU = reserved capacity billed at a fixed hourly rate no matter how many tokens you send; consumption (pay-go) is billed per token.** This tile takes the agents' *measured* token volume in the selected time range, projects it to a full day, and asks: *at this volume, would a PTU reservation be cheaper than pay-go?*\n\nSet **PTU reserved** and **USD per PTU-hour** below, then read the row:\n- **tokens_per_day** — current volume projected to 24h.\n- **breakeven_tokens_day** — the volume where PTU and pay-go cost the same. Below it → consumption wins; above it → PTU wins.\n- **consumption_usd_day** — projected pay-go cost/day at current volume.\n- **ptu_usd_day** — fixed PTU cost/day = PTU × hourly rate × 24 (paid even at zero traffic).\n- **verdict** — which option is cheaper right now.\n\n_Estimate only: PTU has per-deployment minimums (often 15–50 PTU) and monthly/annual reservations are cheaper than hourly. Short sampling windows extrapolate aggressively — widen the time range for a stable number._\n\n**Setting the _USD per PTU-hour_ value** (enter a plain number, no $): it's what you pay to reserve one PTU for one hour, which depends on the billing model — reservations are far cheaper than hourly:\n- **Hourly (no commitment):** ~1.0\n- **Monthly reservation:** ~0.35 (= $ per PTU-month ÷ 730)\n- **Annual reservation:** ~0.30 (= $ per PTU-year ÷ 8760)\n\nRates vary by model and deployment type (Global / Data Zone / Regional Provisioned) and change over time — confirm on the Azure OpenAI pricing page or your EA/CSP price sheet. The default **1.0** is the worst-case (hourly); if consumption still wins at 1.0 it wins even harder at reservation rates._" },
      "name": "hdr-ptu"
    },
    {
      "type": 9,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
